 or with whoever's left.'\n\nThe plasma storm hit at the second waypoint, a wall of fire across the sky. Signal Officer Luz Marek rerouted everything to the shields, hands flying, while Captain Nix Halden threaded the ship through gaps that opened and closed like eyes."}, {'n': 4, 'title': "The Traitor's Price", 'text': "The traitor showed themselves at the third waypoint: the signal officer, paid in promises by Warlord Krell. They seized a distress beacon and ran for the escape pod with Warlord Krell's ships closing in.\n\nCaptain Nix Halden let them live, confined to quarters. 'Warlord Krell trades in hostages,' Captain Nix Halden told the crew. 'We trade in something better.' It was a gamble; the crew's eyes said they knew it.\n\nCaptain Nix Halden laughed for the first time in days. 'All this way,' they said, 'and we were carrying the lock, not the treasure.' Signal Officer Luz Marek was already calculating the wake-up sequence."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Grid Awakens', 'text': "The flagship came on anyway, and Captain Nix Halden met it ship to ship above the burning sky. It was Warlord Krell themselves on the viewscreen, offering one last deal. Captain Nix Halden answered with the engines at full burn.\n\nSilence, then. The grid humming. the Cygnus Expanse safe below. Signal Officer Luz Marek put a hand on Captain Nix Halden's shoulder and said what everyone was thinking: 'We live.'\n\nThey reached the Cygnus Expanse with Warlord Krell's whole fleet behind them, a wall of iron against the stars. Captain Nix Halden broadcast on all bands: 'People of the Cygnus Expanse, wake the grid. Now.'"}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Home Signal', 'text': "And when the next distress call came — as it always does, out in the drift — the engines were already warm. There are always more skies. There is always the Cygnus Expanse, somewhere, needing its heroes.\n\nSignal Officer Luz Marek was offered an admiralty and laughed in the committee's face. 'I have a ship,' they said. It was the highest compliment the crew had ever heard.\n\nCaptain Nix Halden stood on the hull at sunset, watching the Cygnus Expanse turn below. courage among the stars — the stars had taught it, and the crew had proved it, and the grid would remember it."}]}

